cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Stacking Fault Energy Calculator for Austenitic Steels
message: >-
  If you use this calculator, please cite both this repository and the
  source dataset paper by Wang and Xiong (2020).
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Wei
    family-names: Xiong
    affiliation: >-
      Physical Metallurgy and Materials Design Laboratory,
      Department of Mechanical Engineering and Materials Science,
      University of Pittsburgh
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3825-1679'
  - given-names: XinHang
    family-names: Shi
    affiliation: University of Pittsburgh
repository-code: 'https://github.com/DSvL07/sfe-calculator'
url: 'https://dsvl07.github.io/sfe-calculator/'
abstract: >-
  A browser-based calculator that predicts the stacking fault energy of an
  austenitic steel from its composition and temperature. It reports a
  validated uncertainty range and warns when a composition falls outside the
  limits of the training data. Five models are included for comparison; the
  model of record is a linear equation fitted with per-laboratory intercepts.
keywords:
  - stacking fault energy
  - austenitic steel
  - TWIP
  - TRIP
  - machine learning
  - materials informatics
license: MIT
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Stacking fault energy prediction for austenitic steels:
      thermodynamic modeling vs. machine learning
    authors:
      - given-names: Xin
        family-names: Wang
      - given-names: Wei
        family-names: Xiong
    journal: Science and Technology of Advanced Materials
    volume: 21
    issue: 1
    start: 626
    end: 634
    year: 2020
    doi: 10.1080/14686996.2020.1808433
